cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or refer to these results, please cite the paper below."
title: "The encoder, not the bins: decomposing peak-level MS/MS gains"
abstract: >-
  Code and analysis supporting a controlled decomposition of the gain that
  peak-level models show over binned baselines in MS/MS substructure prediction.
  A rounding control separates the encoder from the mass axis; on an openly
  licensed corpus spanning 66 instrument types, 76% of the gain a two-arm
  comparison credits to the representation is the encoder.
